# Adversarial Review — `92819cdf` (Family A + `:content-client`)

**Verdict: REQUEST CHANGES.** The migration is directionally right and no assertion was deleted (509 assertions matches the green pre-refactor baseline `4d0d3e70`, vs 507 in the discarded exploratory attempt). But `src/` was changed to emit a string a test needed, one assertion was weakened in substance while keeping its text, and the evidence is JVM-only from an uncommitted worktree.

**Scope caveat I must state:** I have no shell, so I could not run `git diff --stat 9bc6ebc3..92819cdf`. `.git/logs/HEAD:1031` confirms `9bc6ebc3 → 92819cdf` was a `pull --ff-only`, so the parent is as briefed. The diff-of-record was *supplied* and was produced with `-- src/ test/`, so it cannot show changes outside those trees. I verified its post-image matches the working tree for all four files it touches; "untouched" below is an attestation about that artifact, not a regenerated diff.

---

## Findings

**P1 | `src/cljc/yin/shell/session.cljc:136-140` | Production output authored to satisfy a test string; duplicates the engine-owned notice**
`yin.repl/pending-text` (`src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:1982-1996`) already prints `";; require still pending; lines typed meanwhile run when it completes, (abandon) gives up\n"` (empty-`:links` case) or `";; require pending: <name> (link <id>…); …\n"`, and `recheck-pending*` always calls it when the run stays parked (`repl.cljc:2696-2697`). So `next-text` at `session.cljc:135` is already a pending notice, and the budget-exhausting arm concatenates a second, differently-worded copy. `main/step-all` prints that whole string as one line (`yin/repl/main.cljc:856-858`), so the operator sees:
```
;; require pending: own.m (link [:t0 0], awaiting admission); lines typed meanwhile run when it completes, (abandon) gives up
;; require still pending
```
— and only on the 40th round; rounds 1-39 print one line. The sole consumer is `test/yin/vm/linker/admission_test.cljc:1287`. In that fixture the engine's text is the `"require pending: "` branch (`session/serve:88-91` overwrites `[:pending-run :links]` only when `(:pending linked)` is non-empty, and the 2560 noise requests leave it empty), so **the assertion cannot pass on the engine's message alone** — the literal exists to make it pass. This re-creates the exact defect a sibling dispatch on this branch was opened for (`collab/dao-stream/1794614000000-engineer-fix-dht-head-test.prompt.md:25`: "Printed `;; require still pending; …` twice"), and contradicts this namespace's own contract (`session.cljc:14-19`: "the ordering contract … is the engine's … not something restated here").
*Fix:* delete the `(str text ";; require still pending\n")` arm; return `text` in both. Then serve `:1287`'s intent ("reports its non-blocking state instead of wedging") without authoring surface: either re-point it at the engine's real notice, `(is (str/includes? text "require pending"))` — the state half is already pinned by `(is (some? (:pending-run successor)))` at `:1285` — or, if exhaustion wording must be distinguishable, export it from `yin.repl` (owner of `pending-text`) and reference it, never re-type it.

**P1 | verification coverage | The changed production tick path was never run where it actually runs**
`session/recheck-on-tick` reaches production only via `shell.main/composition:58` → `main/composition-recheck:370` → `step-all:855`. The handback's four runs are all JVM-only and none includes `test/yin/repl/dht_process_test.clj` — the `^:slow` test that spawns a real JVM publisher **and a real Node reader** (`bb build:yin-repl-node`) over loopback and `await-line`s their transcripts (`:22-23, :209-211, :300-301, :473-489`). No `:cljs` or `:cljd` lane ran at all; on those hosts the two `^:slow` e2e tests also need `DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1` (`test/dao/test_slow.cljc:17-24`). And per the handback itself: *"Commit SHA: unavailable. `git add` failed: … Read-only file system"* — so every quoted green run is from an **uncommitted worktree on a shared `~/ci` clone**, not from `92819cdf`.
*Fix:* re-attest at the committed SHA with `git status --porcelain` clean before and after, and run `clojure -M:test -i :slow -n yin.repl.dht-process-test` (jupiter) plus the node/dart lanes over `yin.vm.linker.admission-test` and `yin.vm.linker.dht-end-to-end-test` with `DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1` (shiva).

**P2 | `src/cljc/yin/shell/session.cljc:125-140` | Two independent `link-round-budget` loops nested; ~40× per-tick amplification**
`left` starts at `repl/link-round-budget` (40 — `repl.cljc:79-85`, documented as "how many serve-and-run rounds **one evaluation** drives"). Each iteration runs `serve` → `serve-links` (one `link/round` at `serve-budget`) **and** `serve-services` (budget 64), then `repl/recheck-pending` → `drive-links`, which has its *own* 40-round loop (`repl.cljc:1927`). Worst case per host tick: 40 serve rounds (2560 link requests + 2560 query calls) and up to 40×40 VM runs, vs 1 + ≤40 before. `admission_test.cljc:1271-1274` now pins the amplification as intended (`answered` = `serve-budget × link-round-budget` = 2560) and `:1310` pins `@rounds` = 40. The constant's own docstring scopes it to one evaluation and says the budget "is reached only by a link that stays `:pending`" — reusing it for a host tick conflates two bounds so neither can be tuned.
*Fix:* add a distinct `yin.shell.session/tick-round-budget` (start 1-4) for the composition's continuation, leave `repl/link-round-budget` to the engine's drive, and document the product as the per-tick ceiling. If a 40-round same-tick drain is genuinely wanted, record it in `docs/design/yin.repl.dht-composition.md` §7 and bound the *total*, not each factor.

**P2 | `src/cljc/yin/shell/session.cljc:104` + `:130-131, :136` | Composition-wide `:progress?` fed to the engine as run-specific `initial-progress`; a parked run's `:checks` can never advance**
`serve` answers `:progress? (or (:progress? linked) (:progress? served))`. `link/round`'s flag is true when "at least one response **or admission question** was appended" (`yin/vm/linker/pair.cljc:461-462, :508, :587-588`) — including a response to another VM's request, or to noise. That flag is passed straight through as `initial-progress true` (`:131`); `drive-links` with `initial-progress` true always returns `progress?` true (runs the VM on `initial?`, carries `true` into the recur — `repl.cljc:1917-1975`), so `recheck-pending*` takes `(if progress? 0 (inc …))` and pins `:checks` at 0 (`repl.cljc:2688`) — against the documented contract that `:checks` counts "this pending run's re-checks that made **no progress**" (`repl.cljc:2664-2667`). Consequence: a `:fn` link policy that abandons after N fruitless re-checks **can never fire** on a composition with any background traffic, and the same flag is the loop's continuation condition, so unrelated traffic alone drives all 40 rounds. `admission_test.cljc:1288` and `:1256` now enshrine `:checks` = 0 in exactly that situation.
*Fix:* scope the flag to the parked run — have `serve` also answer `:run-progress?`, true only when a response landed for one of `(get-in engine [:pending-run :links])`' `:yin.link/id`s or an admission answer matched one of its `:admission` ids — and use *that* for both `initial-progress` and the loop condition. Keep `:progress?` for the host's cadence bit.

**P2 | `test/yin/vm/linker/admission_test.cljc:627-632` + `:987` | The `identical?` assertion is now satisfied by the fixture, not by production code**
`tick!` returns `[(if (= state next) state next) text]` — when the value is unchanged it hands back the *input object*, so `(is (identical? state state'))` in `a-late-answer-completes-the-require-with-no-typed-line-test` ("an unrelated load event re-checks nothing") is true by construction. Pre-migration it was load-bearing: `yin.repl/recheck-on-tick` returns the identical map when the linker did not move (`repl.cljc:2765-2768`). Identity is now *unachievable* across the shell boundary — `shell.linker/install` unconditionally `assoc`s (`yin/shell/linker.cljc:69-71`) — so the honest migration was to change the assertion, not manufacture the identity. Secondary: `=` is an unsound "nothing moved" oracle here because the state holds mutable media (ring buffers, mesh handles) that compare by identity, so `tick!` can report unchanged while a medium was written in place; and it deep-compares engine + DHT node on every tick (`settle:658-673` calls it up to 40×).
*Fix:* drop the fabrication, return `(assoc (:engine s) :node (:node s))`, and restate `:987` as what the boundary can guarantee — `(is (= state state'))` alongside the existing `(is (nil? text'))` and `(is (= (:pending-run state) (:pending-run state')))`. Record the identity→equality downgrade explicitly in the findings instead of hiding it behind an unchanged assertion count.

**P2 | `admission_test.cljc:634-648` vs `main.cljc:861-869` | Three fixture drive policies for "evaluate one line", none of them production's**
Production drives exactly **one** composition round after input, and only when the input newly parked a run. The fixtures each invent their own: `admission_test/type!` loops up to 40 (`:634-648`); `dht_test/eval-shell` loops to a hard-coded 32 (`test/yin/repl/dht_test.cljc:96-110`); `dht_head_test/type!` loops to 32 then adds a string-matched extra re-check (`test/yin/repl/dht_head_test.cljc:167-183`); `dht_end_to_end_test/eval-at` does one round (`:155-163`). So the Family-A acceptance instrument drives the composition 40× harder than the shipped host: a require that settles only on round 2..40 passes the fixture while the operator's shell still needs 39 more ticks.
*Fix:* promote one bounded "evaluate a line and drive the composition" entry into `src/cljc/yin/shell/session.cljc` (mirroring `recheck-after-input`), have `main/step-all` and all four fixtures call it, and keep the bound in one named constant.

**P3 | `admission_test.cljc:627-648` | Fixture drops the transport half it is meant to carry**
Both `tick!` and `type!` rebuild `(session/make (dissoc state :node) (:node state) a)` per call and keep only `(assoc (:engine s) :node (:node s))`, discarding `:awaiting`, `:key`, `:limits`. `session/make`'s docstring says `:awaiting` "starts empty: the composition carries it across ticks exactly as it carries the node" (`session.cljc:38-42`); `transport-state` exists for exactly this (`:49-66`). Resetting it per tick means a `yin.link/publish` parked on its local publication completion loses its correlation and would be re-committed or never answered (`yin/shell/query.cljc:301-320, :392-403`). Latent today (no admission-test scenario publishes), but this is the fixture that should have caught it — and `dht_end_to_end_test` *does* carry `:session` correctly (`:127-131, :155-162`), so the two disagree. It also keeps `:node` **inside** the engine map, which `session.cljc:11-13` and `main/session-of` (`main.cljc:325-329`) both forbid.
*Fix:* mirror the e2e adapter (store `session/transport-state` beside the engine and thread it), or build the fixture on `main/boot` + `shell.main/composition` + `main/session-of`/`with-session` as `dht_head_test.cljc:89-95` already does.

**P3 | `admission_test.cljc:640-646`, `dht_end_to_end_test.cljc:162` | `(or t text)` discards earlier text instead of accumulating**
`type!`'s recur carries `(or t text)` and `eval-at` carries `(or resumed text)`, so the first re-check that produces any text throws away `repl/eval-input`'s. `settle:658-673` and `main/step-all:856-858, :880-883` both accumulate. Every assertion reading these as *subjects* happens to be safe today — `an-untrusted-import-is-refused-at-the-shell-with-no-load-test:756-760` exits before any re-check (`:pending-run` nil), and `a-trusted-import-records…:703` reaches `(is (= "43" …))` with nothing parked — but a refusal printed by `eval-input` followed by any pending notice would be silently overwritten. `dht_head_test.cljc:172-181` already needed a string-matched patch for this shape.
*Fix:* accumulate (`(str text t)` / `(str text resumed)`), or return both and let each assertion name the half it means.

**P3 | `test/yin/repl/dht_test.cljc:1709-1713` | New `:content-client` pin accepts any exception, and its label over-claims**
`(is (some? (refusal-of #(create-state {:index-store-spec (dht-spec dir {}) :content-client {}}))))` asserts only that *something* threw. The intended refusal is `shell.store/open`'s `"A composed store cannot use a second content source"` (`src/cljc/yin/shell/store.cljc:105-107`), which fires on the **first** `let` binding — before `shell.dht/open`. So the follow-up `(testing "and the client refusal left the directory unlocked" …)` is unfalsifiable for release-on-failure: nothing was ever acquired. If a future `:content-client` shape validation threw first, the pin would keep passing while the composition guard became dead code. (`{}` is truthy on all three hosts, so the guard does fire — that part is sound.)
*Fix:* pin the reason using the convention already at `:246-247` — `(is (str/includes? (ex-message (refusal-of …)) "second content source"))` — and either rename the `testing` to what it proves ("the refused open left the directory free for a later open") or add a case that fails *after* acquisition so release-on-failure is observed.

**P3 | `test/yin/vm/linker/dht_end_to_end_test.cljc:227-231` | Dead, self-referential adapter in `hydrate`**
`(assoc (:session (get-in % [:shells k])) :engine (get-in % [:shells k]))` — but `repl.dht/admitting?` and `refusal` read `(:node session)` and nothing else (`src/cljc/yin/shell/dht.cljc:1335-1357`), and `(:session s)` already carries `:node`, kept in sync with `:dht` at `:104-105` and `:129-131`. The `:engine` assoc is inert, and the value installed is the whole shell map — which contains `:session` — so it builds a self-referential session for no reader. If either function ever reads `:engine`, it will see one still carrying `:session`/`:dht`, unlike the `(dissoc s :session :dht)` engine every other call site passes.
*Fix:* `(repl.dht/admitting? (:session (get-in % [:shells k])))` / `(repl.dht/refusal (:session (get-in w [:shells k])))`, or reuse `step-world:127`'s `transport`.

**P3 | `src/cljc/yin/shell/session.cljc:108-122` | `recheck-on-tick` docstring now false on both claims**
It still reads "One host tick: serve both media, then let the engine re-check a run it has parked. Answers `[session' text]` **exactly as** the engine's own `yin.repl/recheck-on-tick` does", plus "A round that made progress resumes the run … a round that made none leaves the resume to a matching completion." The body at `:125-140` serves and re-checks up to 40× per tick and can return text the engine's never produces (`:139`).
*Fix:* state the bounded continuation (the bound, what continues it, and that the caller's `events` are offered inward on at most one round), and either give the new constant its own doc or note in `repl/link-round-budget`'s that it is now shared.

**P3 | `src/cljc/yin/shell/session.cljc:137` | Tick events dropped when the first round reports progress, then hard-coded to `[]`**
On iteration 1 with `(:progress? served)` true, the `repl/recheck-on-tick` arm is not taken, so `completion/completion-events` is never computed and the caller's transport/follower events are discarded; the recur binds `events` to `[]`, so a later iteration taking the no-progress arm (`:132-133`) translates an empty vector. `dht_end_to_end_test/step-world:129` feeds real `:loaded`/hydration events here every reading. Not a wedge (the composition's own `link/round` reads the node directly, and the next tick brings fresh events), but it silently converts an event-driven resume into a poll — the behaviour `repl/recheck-on-tick`'s docstring (`repl.cljc:2748-2760`) says the translation exists to prevent.
*Fix:* translate and offer `events` inward exactly once before the continuation loop, or clear them only after a round that actually passed them to `repl/recheck-on-tick`.

**P3 | `admission_test.cljc:731-735, :849-853, :980-984, :1010, :1062, :1502-1505` + `:634-648` | Stale continuation indentation and over-long lines**
Every `repl/recheck-on-tick` → `tick!` swap kept the old column alignment for the longer symbol, leaving continuations over-indented by ~16 spaces; `type!`'s new body carries 108- and 111-char lines against the file's ~80-col convention. `.cljstyle` enables `:indentation` and `:whitespace`, and `bb.edn` has no lint task, so nothing catches this — but `cljstyle fix` on the next seat's run will produce unrelated churn in this file. Blank-line spacing is fine (max 2 consecutive, per `.cljstyle`).
*Fix:* re-flow the six `tick!` call sites and wrap `type!`'s `let` bindings.

