## Confirmations requested by the brief

**Gate A — intact.** `dao\.jing\.dht|yin\.link\.dht|yin\.shell\.dht|datagram` → **0 matches** in `src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc` and **0** in `src/cljc/yin/repl/`. The only `yin.shell.*` mentions in `repl.cljc` are two docstring cross-references (`:1110`, `:2758-2759`) to `yin.shell.linker`/`yin.shell.completion` — outside the Gate A pattern and creating no require edge. `session.cljc`'s require list is unchanged by this commit, so the `dao.host.gate-test` closure rooted at `yin.repl.main` (`test/dao/host/gate_test.clj:90`; `docs/design/host-boundary/closure-*.edn`, last updated at `e181a633`) needs no update.

**`yin/repl.cljc` and `yin/repl/` untouched — per the supplied artifact.** The diff-of-record has hunks for exactly four files (`session.cljc`, `dht_test.cljc`, `admission_test.cljc`, `dht_end_to_end_test.cljc`), none under those paths; the post-image matches the working tree. See the scope caveat above: this is not a diff I regenerated, and the `-- src/ test/` filter would hide changes to `docs/`, `bb.edn`, or `deps.edn`.

**`.cljc` portability — statically sound on `:clj`/`:cljs`/`:cljd`, but unproven by any run.**
- `session.cljc:125-140` uses only `loop/recur`, `str`, `dec`, `>`, `=`, `or`, `and`; no reader conditionals, no host interop. `repl/link-round-budget` is a plain `def`.
- `tick!`/`type!` use only portable core fns. `traced-tick:1082` keeps `#?(:cljd … :cljs … :clj …)` with `:cljd` **first**, which `.cljstyle`'s header comment says is load-bearing (cljd host-eval also matches `:clj`).
- Both `with-redefs` spies (`:1093-1096`, `:1301-1306`) are now 3-arity `(fn [value node budget] …)`, matching every production call site: `shell.linker/serve-links:52-56` always calls `link/round` with three args, and `link/round`'s 2-arity (`interpreter.cljc:299`) delegates to the 3-arity. No ArityException path.
- New requires `yin.shell.main` / `yin.shell.session` are both `.cljc` and already loaded on all three lanes by `dht_test.cljc`. `shell.main/composition` is a constant map; only `-main` is host-guarded (`shell/main.cljc:70-90`).
- `dht_end_to_end_test`'s switch to `main/boot` is already exercised on all lanes (`dht_test.cljc:785, :832, :1002, :1741`; `dht_head_test.cljc:95`). `host/websocket` is a pure selector with per-build shadows (`yin/repl/host.cljc:21-40`), so `main/boot` opens no socket eagerly. Dropping the `yin.repl.frontends` require is correct — zero remaining references in the file.

**Assertion preservation, `admission_test.cljc`.** All five named properties survive structurally: inheritance (`:728-753`, still compares the child VM's `module/module-entry` against the recorded admission), tick-rollback (`:1194-1243`, all four modes, `settled-successor:1136` whole-successor equality plus the JVM `(peek _successors)` pin), trusted-import (`:703-727` and `boot-keeps-declared-authority…:785-804`), answer-alone progress (`:995-1012`), idle-tick (`:1246-1256`, including the JVM-only `(is (= [:round :drain] _trace))`). `assert-handoff:1115-1128` is unchanged, and `one-tick-hands-external-and-snapshot-progress…:1161` still pins the exact whole successor. **The one substantive weakening is `:987`** (P2 above) — invisible in the 509 count.

**Assertion preservation, `dht_end_to_end_test.cljc`.** No `is` deleted or altered; the migration is entirely at fixture level (`shell-at:88-107`, `step-world:122-140`, `eval-at:155-163`, `hydrate:220-232`). Unlike `admission_test`, this fixture carries the full transport half (`:awaiting`/`:key`/`:limits`) across ticks and keeps `:dht`/`:session` in sync — the better of the two migrations. Its four non-`^:slow` deftests (`:304, :324, :378, :487, :512`) ran in the handback's command 4, so `publish-world`/`hydrate`/`require-at`/`eval-at` are genuinely exercised on the JVM.

